{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775331151-yI5ttG9I1sGiR3jOxsyI","role":"assistant","created":1775331163,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The question asks for \"saving note redemption rate out of the average amount outstanding\". This means we need to calculate:\n- Redemption Rate = Redemptions / Average Amount Outstanding\n\nFor average amount outstanding, I need to calculate the average of the beginning and ending balance for each year.\n\nFor Calendar year 1980:\n- Beginning amount outstanding (at start of 1980, which is end of 1979): 352 million\n- Ending amount outstanding (at end of 1980): 300 million\n- Average = (352 + 300) / 2 = 326 million\n- Redemptions = 71 million\n- Redemption rate = 71 / 326 = 0.21779... = 21.78%\n\nFor Calendar year 1981:\n- Beginning amount outstanding (at start of 1981, which is end of 1980): 300 million\n- Ending amount outstanding (at end of 1981): 269 million\n- Average = (300 + 269) / 2 = 284.5 million\n- Redemptions = 51 million\n- Redemption rate = 51 / 284.5 = 0.17926... = 17.93%\n\nAbsolute difference = |21.78 - 17.93| = 3.85 percentage points\n\nLet me be more precise with the calculation:\n- 1980: 71/326 = 0.217791 = 21.7791%\n- 1981: 51/284.5 = 0.179261 = 17.9261%\n- Difference = 21.7791 - 17.9261 = 3.8530 percentage points\n\nRounded to the nearest hundredth: 3.85\n\nLet me verify the numbers in the table one more time. Looking at the Calendar years section:\n- 1979: Amount outstanding = 352\n- 1980: Redemptions = 71, Amount outstanding = 300\n- 1981: Redemptions = 51, Amount outstanding = 269\n\nSo for 1980:\n- Beginning: 352\n\n\n- Ending: 300\n- Average: (352 + 300) / 2 = 326\n- Rate: 71/326 = 0.21779... = 21.78%\n\nFor 1981:\n- Beginning: 300\n- Ending: 269\n- Average: (300 + 269) / 2 = 284.5\n- Rate: 51/284.5 = 0.17926... = 17.93%\n\nThe difference between these rates is 3.85 percentage points.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_beeac4cb89cc496ea58c334c","toolCall":{"status":"succe